Turning the second factor on: the QR code of the otpauth URI, the secret
for an app that cannot read one, and the form for the first code.  The
page is not cached (Cache-Control: no-store), since it holds the secret.

qr is written with |safe: the escaping of a URL attribute turns every
scheme but http, https and mailto into #ZgotmplZ, and qr
is made by the server alone, data:image/png;base64, and base64 digits,
with no quote and nothing of the request in it.
-#}
{% extends "templates/base.jinja" %}
{% block title %}Two-factor{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<p><img alt="QR code for the authenticator app" src="{{ qr|safe }}"></p>
<p>secret: <code class="secret">{{ secret }}</code></p>
<form method="post" action="/totp">
<input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{ csrf }}">
<input name="code" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="one-time-code" maxlength="6">
<button>Turn on</button>
</form>
{% endblock %}
